From 9ee45eec42d826387160b44f571beea8b9f497e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:23:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-302: IQ4_NL q8_1 integer-dot mat-vec + expert-gather
 twin, opt-in GGML_ARIFI_IQ4NL_MMVQ=1 (every n)

Route B of lane 302. IQ4_NL (the qwen4exp ffn_down_exps type, 39 tensors) had no q8_1 MMVQ shader. It now joins
the legacy-quant MMVQ arm with Q4_0 geometry: same 18-byte block and nibble order, the nibbles index the signed
int8 kvalues LUT (CUDA vec_dot_iq4_nl_q8_1: d_a * d_b * int-dot, no ds.y term). Pipelines: MUL_MAT [w][cols],
MUL_MAT_ID, and a MUL_MAT_ID_GATHER twin of mul_mat_vecq.comp (slot-major order, B_COL/D_COL) so the q8_1 path
keeps the gather's L2 reuse at n > 1.

Routing: ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq_impl decides IQ4_NL first, at EVERY n, MUL_MAT and MUL_MAT_ID alike (no new
row-count dependence, lane 300). Default OFF (f32 dequant, the engine of record path). This is a precision
change (activations quantized to q8_1), not byte-identical to the f32 path; quality is measured (KL + top-1),
not assumed. Startup notice: "ggml_vulkan: iq4_nl mmvq: ON|OFF".

Lane: lane-302
(cherry picked from commit 9673f054d5851c03be8c529515dfb60b1fb2fffa)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-302); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - no served number for this commit in the release ledger or the commit message
